id: pm-oskdmu
title: "ADR amendment: extensible durable agent provenance dimensions and privacy boundaries"
description: "Amend pm-qwuber so durable, bounded, non-secret provenance can add declared dimensions such as reasoning effort and explicit session role without serializing raw session identifiers; define source precedence, absence semantics, privacy, compatibility, and conformance gates."
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: architecture,"area:sdk",history,identity,privacy,provenance
created_at: "2026-07-27T04:36:34.996Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T06:23:38.799Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T06:23:26.580Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The decision distinguishes durable descriptive provenance from transient session identifiers and authorization identity; Reasoning effort and explicit role/topic have declared bounded sources, absence semantics, and privacy rules; Raw session IDs remain transient while privacy-safe agent_instance continues to distinguish concurrent agents; Older history remains readable and every new dimension is optional and schema-gated; The decision defines a conformance gate that prevents declared dimensions from remaining inert"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make automatic agent provenance extensible without weakening privacy or compatibility
value: Agents remain zero-configuration while history records the context needed to understand who acted and under what reasoning profile
why_now: The current accepted ADR requires an amendment before pm-itsjf0 can change the durable identity shape
parent: pm-m2u1
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Accepted and documented the extensible durable provenance amendment, including precedence, absence semantics, backward compatibility, privacy boundaries, and conformance reporting."
expected_result: The architecture decision clearly separates descriptive provenance from authorization and transient session identity.
actual_result: "The ADR and operator guide define optional schema-gated dimensions, hashed instances, raw-session privacy limits, compatibility behavior, and inert-source gates."
